# Reference Section Contents

Grammar reference lookup for cases, pronouns, articles, verbs, adjectives, and prepositions.

## Route Structure

```
/reference                    Redirects to first tab
/reference/:tab               Grammar reference by topic
```

## Routes

<route path="/reference/:tab">
<purpose>Grammar reference lookup organised by topic</purpose>
<file>src/routes/reference/$tab.tsx</file>
<data-source>Static: hardcoded grammar content in component files</data-source>
<tabs>
- cases-pronouns: Cases overview and pronoun paradigms
- nouns-articles: Article paradigms and gender agreement
- adjectives: Adjective agreement patterns
- prepositions: Preposition + case combinations
- verbs: Verb conjugation patterns
</tabs>
</route>

<tab route="/reference/cases-pronouns">
<purpose>Foundation of Greek grammar - cases and pronouns</purpose>
<file>src/routes/reference/tabs/cases-pronouns.tsx</file>
<components>
- CasesSection (components/cases-section.tsx)
- PronounsSection (components/pronouns-section.tsx)
</components>
<displays>
- Hero: "Foundation of Greek grammar" - Ποιος; Τι; Ποιου;
- Cases overview: nominative (who?), accusative (what?), genitive (whose?)
- Pronoun paradigm tables showing all forms by person/number
- Pronoun decision guide (subject vs object vs possessive)
- Practice CTA linking to /practice/speed?focus=pronouns
</displays>
</tab>

<tab route="/reference/nouns-articles">
<purpose>Article paradigms and noun agreement</purpose>
<file>src/routes/reference/tabs/nouns-articles.tsx</file>
<components>
- AgreementSection (components/agreement-section.tsx)
- MovableNuSection (components/agreement-section.tsx)
</components>
<displays>
- Hero: "Articles and nouns" - ο, η, το → τον, την, το
- Definite article paradigm table (masculine/feminine/neuter × nominative/accusative/genitive × singular/plural)
- Gender agreement rules
- Movable nu (ν) rule explanation
- Practice CTA linking to /practice/speed?focus=articles
</displays>
</tab>

<tab route="/reference/adjectives">
<purpose>Adjective agreement patterns</purpose>
<file>src/routes/reference/tabs/adjectives.tsx</file>
<components>
- AdjectivesSection (components/adjectives-section.tsx)
</components>
<displays>
- Hero: "Words that describe" - ο καλός, η καλή, το καλό
- Adjective agreement paradigm (same pattern as articles)
- Common adjective examples
- Practice CTA linking to /practice/speed?focus=adjectives
</displays>
</tab>

<tab route="/reference/prepositions">
<purpose>Preposition usage and case requirements</purpose>
<file>src/routes/reference/tabs/prepositions.tsx</file>
<components>
- PrepositionsSection (components/prepositions-section.tsx)
- PrepositionNavigator (components/preposition-navigator.tsx)
</components>
<displays>
- Hero: "Connect words and ideas" - σε, από, για, με
- The big four prepositions (σε, από, για, με)
- Case requirements for each preposition
- Usage examples and contractions (σε + τον → στον)
- Practice CTA linking to /practice/speed?focus=prepositions
</displays>
</tab>

<tab route="/reference/verbs">
<purpose>Verb conjugation patterns and tenses</purpose>
<file>src/routes/reference/tabs/verbs.tsx</file>
<components>
- VerbsSection (components/verbs-section.tsx)
</components>
<displays>
- Hero: "Verb conjugation patterns" - κάνω, κάνεις, κάνει...
- Verb family overview (-ω, -άω/-ώ, deponent)
- Present tense paradigm tables
- Tense overview (present, past, future)
- Practice CTA linking to /practice/speed?focus=verbs
</displays>
</tab>

## Component Library

The reference section uses modular components for grammar content:

<components>
<component file="components/cases-section.tsx">
Case system overview with nominative/accusative/genitive explanations
</component>

<component file="components/pronouns-section.tsx">
Full pronoun paradigm tables with PronounParadigmTable component
</component>

<component file="components/pronoun-paradigm-table.tsx">
Reusable table for displaying pronoun forms by person/number
</component>

<component file="components/pronoun-decision-guide.tsx">
Flowchart for choosing correct pronoun form
</component>

<component file="components/agreement-section.tsx">
Article paradigm table and gender agreement rules
</component>

<component file="components/adjectives-section.tsx">
Adjective agreement patterns mirroring article paradigms
</component>

<component file="components/prepositions-section.tsx">
Preposition usage with PrepositionNavigator for browsing
</component>

<component file="components/preposition-navigator.tsx">
Interactive navigator for exploring preposition combinations
</component>

<component file="components/verbs-section.tsx">
Verb family paradigms and conjugation patterns
</component>
</components>
